OL,7,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,8,     GSir Antonio and the LSO plays
OL,9,     GTchaikovsky's 4th Symphony and
OL,10,     Gcontinue their exploration of the
OL,11,     Gmusic of Vaughan Williams with
OL,12,     Ghis ravishing Flos Campi and Dona
OL,13,     Gnobis pacem.
OL,14,G2145FThe Essay: Accompanying Austen
OL,15,     GAntonia Quirke speaks to
OL,16,     Gcomposers who've scored original
OL,17,     Gmusic for Austen adaptations
OL,18,     Gabout their musical choices and
OL,19,     Gabout the music Austen enjoyed
OL,20,     Gtoo. Today: Adrian Johnston.
